The **service_snapshot "no_addresses" result was a false positive**: it queried the bare hostname `srv1` (without FQDN suffix). With no `search` or `domain` directive in `/etc/resolv.conf`, the system resolver sends that bare name to an authoritative-only BIND server (`recursion no`), which correctly REFUSES it. That is not a fault — it is expected authoritative-DNS behavior.

Phase A, B, and D triage are all clean. No anomaly survives the full pass.

